<title>AUSTRALIA: W. Australia signs waste paper recycling contracts.</title>
<headline>W. Australia signs waste paper recycling contracts.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-06-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Western Australian government agencies were leading the way in reducing the amount of recyclable paper sent to landfills, state Environment Minister Cheryl Edwardes said in a statement.</p>
<p>The government's Department of Contract and Management Services had awarded a new paper recycling contract jointly to Austissue Pty Ltd and Paper Recycling Industries, she said.</p>
<p>&quot;The new contract aims to maximise the amount of waste recycled by state government agencies and reduce the volume of waste paper dumped in landfills,&quot; she said.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
